#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:IllFramedPValueShape (Rule I1): a math:PValue
# whose test arm is satisfied via the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is —
# NOT via a direct math:testStatistic on the p-value itself. The p-value carries a
# math:nullHypothesis, a math:nullDistribution that is a PARAMETERIZED
# math:SamplingDistribution (a math:Distribution: normal family + mean/stddev
# parameterization, one math:DistributionParameter per required role, matching the
# probability.ttl idiom), a math:alternativeSidedness that IS one of the six lawful
# math:Sidedness individuals (math:twoSidedAlternative), and math:pValue → a FRAMED
# math:ProbabilityValue. The math:Statistic instead lives on ex:theHypothesisTest via
# math:testStatistic — a lawful placement, since math:testStatistic's domain is a
# math:HypothesisTest OR a math:PValue (stated in prose in module.ttl). Because the
# test arm's disjunction ("a direct math:testStatistic, and/or the math:HypothesisTest
# whose math:pValue it is") is satisfied by the SECOND branch, and every other arm
# (null hypothesis, null distribution, tail-or-sidedness) is present, the SPARQL frame
# gate stays SILENT even though the p-value names no direct math:testStatistic; because
# the sidedness is lawful, the sh:in gate stays SATISFIED. This exercises the
# HypothesisTest path of the shape's test arm, which a direct-testStatistic-only fixture
# (conformance-fixtures/pvalue-well-framed.ttl) never reaches. The p-value's magnitude
# 3/100 is carried, per the exact-rational discipline, as a math:RationalValue with a
# gmeow:hasReferenceFrame, so its value satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape
# (0 ≤ 3/100 ≤ 1), math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (a reference frame),
# math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape, and math:RationalValueShape. The null distribution
# is well-formed, so the P6a/P6b/P7 distribution gates stay silent. It MUST raise NO
# failure class.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecPValueHypothesisTestFramed).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:htTestPValue a math:PValue ;
    math:nullHypothesis ex:noEffectNull ;
    math:nullDistribution ex:tNullDistribution ;
    math:alternativeSidedness math:twoSidedAlternative ;
    math:pValue ex:pValueMagnitude .

ex:theHypothesisTest a math:HypothesisTest ;
    math:pValue ex:htTestPValue ;
    math:testStatistic ex:hypTestStatistic .

ex:hypTestStatistic a math:Statistic .
ex:noEffectNull a math:NullHypothesis .

# The null distribution: the distribution of the statistic UNDER the null, a
# parameterized sampling distribution (a math:Distribution) with family + convention.
ex:tNullDistribution a math:SamplingDistribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:normalFamily ;
    math:distributionParameterization ex:meanStddevParameterization ;
    math:hasDistributionParameter ex:meanParam , ex:stddevParam .

ex:normalFamily a math:DistributionFamily .

ex:meanStddevParameterization a math:DistributionParameterization ;
    math:requiresParameterRole ex:meanRole , ex:stddevRole .

ex:meanRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .
ex:stddevRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .

ex:meanParam a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:meanRole .

ex:stddevParam a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:stddevRole .

# The p-value magnitude: a FRAMED probability value, exact 3/100 = 0.03 in [0, 1].
ex:pValueMagnitude a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 3 ;         # 3/100 = 0.03, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 100 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:samplingFrame .

ex:samplingFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/pValueMagnitude> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
